      "content": "It seems like the core of the issue is that the dissent's argument basically can't be defended within a proper legal framework. Given how much it clashes with the textualist requirements, are there any serious legal scholars who would argue that their position is actually valid, or is it generally accepted that their approach is just a form of judicial overreach?",
